hadiths[1]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1321","Muhammad bin Amr bin Al-Abbas narrated to us in Baghdad, and his origin is Basra. Sa’id bin Amir told us, on the authority of Abu Amir Al-Khazzaz, Abu Qalabat Al-Jarmi: We set out with Anas to go to the corner. He said: We passed by a mosque and the morning prayer came. Anas said: If only we had prayed in this place. The mosque. Some people came to the other mosque. They said: Which mosque? Then we mentioned a mosque. He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: “A time will come upon the people when they will brag about mosques and will not inhabit them without A little, or he said: They live in it a little. Abu Bakr said: Al-Zawiya is a palace near Basra about two farsangs away."
